 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It means the wheel hub is wobbling around in the dropout. A bike shop puts the pedals on and adjusts the brakes and bike stand, so the wheel is straight. He' being helpful, but he should warn you before he leaves. If the wheel is damaged, it' better to sort it out now while you can still ride home. That's often caused by weak back muscles or poor seating. Try sitting on both sides and moving the renting bike's seat around. A bike shop will fit it for free if it's damaged. They' usually check it for free, too. It' worth asking at the shop you mention.",
